  ["investigation-only finding: reusing local-murakumo's existing USDC/Gnosis-Safe treasury
    rail for club-shinshi's frozen creator monetization (PPV/subscriptions/tips) is NOT a
    safe drop-in reuse -- it conflicts with two already-decided portfolio ADRs
    (2606010100's fiat-first/crypto-second sequencing + on-chain-code boundary for the
    shinshi repo, and 2606011400's etzhayyim-resident-only on-chain settlement pattern
    where gftd is never merchant-of-record/custodian)"
   "new concrete risk identified: treasury commingling -- local-murakumo's Safe is a
    freezable-USDC address; sharing it across two unrelated business lines (murakumo
    compute credits + shinshi creator payouts) means a compliance freeze on one freezes
    the other's unrelated revenue too"
   "crypto does not remove the adult-business PSP problem, it moves it to whichever fiat
    on-ramp provider is used (their KYB/AUP typically also excludes adult businesses,
    same as Stripe) -- the fiat-rail search (CCBill/Verotel/Epoch/Segpay) already
    identified in ADR-2606010100 remains necessary regardless"
   "recommendation: do not deprioritize the fiat PSP search; if a crypto rail is pursued,
    use a separate shinshi-specific treasury, not local-murakumo's; follow the existing
    etzhayyim-resident on-chain pattern rather than inventing a third settlement shape;
    vendor/PSP selection and compliance certification are explicitly out of scope (business
    and legal decisions, not engineering ones)"]
